dct_description_sm:
For each fish (ID), 2 trials were done to measure the time spent on each side:
-Control 1: Uninfected conspecifics VS No fish;
-Control 2: Infected conspecifics VS No fish;
-Treatment: Infected conspecifics VS Uninfected conspecific.

METADATA:
-ID: Identification of the focal fish; 
-Lake: Origin of the focal fish (Triton or Cromwell);
-Treatment: Experiment set up (Control 1, Control 2 or Treatment);
-Tank: Holding tank in lab;
-Trial: First or second focal fish trial (1 or 2);
-Temp_exp: Temperature of the arena during trials (Celcius) ;
-Time_exp: time of the day the test to place (am or pm);
-Side_Fish: Side of the arena where stimuli fish are (for Control 1 and 2);
-Side_Uninf: Side of the arena where uninfected stimuli fish are (for Treatment);
-TL: Total length of focal fish (mm);
-SL: Standard length of focal fish (mm);
-Mass = Mass of focal fish (g);
-a = Constant in the equation Mass = a * SL^b;
-b = Constant in the equation Mass = a * SL^b;
-Spleen_mass: Spleen mass of the focal fish (g);
-Sex: Sex of the focal fish (Male, Female, NA);
-BS_tot: Total number of blackspot parasites; 
-BT_tot: Total number of bass tapeworm parasites;
-Other: Total number of yellow grub and nematode parasites; 
-Total_parasites: Total number of parasites;
-Parasites_density: Total_parasites / Mass; 
-Infected_zone: Time spent with infected conspecifics (s);
-Uninfected_zone: Time spent with uninfected conspecifics (s); 
-None_zone: Time spent with no fish (Control only) (s);
-Neutral_zone: Time spent in the center of the arena (Visual cues only) (s);
-Total_time: Duration of the trial;
-Shoal: Number of the shoal used as stimulus;
-Notes: Any notes taken during the experiment or the dissection.
